# PIC-2D steady-state v5 (preregistered 25 um ladder point): results stay untracked until the run ends
# (results-only commit adds the negations); the non-evidentiary shakedown directory is never tracked.
# Launch 1 (RTX 5090, PID 43572, lock at 69ff435d) was WITHDRAWN by the user at 21:26:48 AEST 2026-09-04 (compute moved
# to the Lambda H100): its record - execution lock, run state, checkpoint metadata + sha256 sidecars, status/series,
# log/err/pid - is tracked under results-launch1-withdrawn/ (not a result, not a failure); the checkpoint arrays
# (107 MB + the 1.9 MB field anchor) and the 40 frames stay untracked; results/ is reserved for the H100 execution
modern/experiments/pic2d_cft_steady_state_v5/results*/
!modern/experiments/pic2d_cft_steady_state_v5/results-launch1-withdrawn/
!modern/experiments/pic2d_cft_steady_state_v5/results-launch1-withdrawn/checkpoint/
modern/experiments/pic2d_cft_steady_state_v5/results-launch1-withdrawn/frames/
# PIC-2D design mini-sweep v1 (preregistered channel-33um option): per-design results/<design>-<option>/ stay untracked
# until a run ends (results-only commit adds the negations); the shakedown and MPS-replay scratch directories are never tracked
modern/experiments/pic2d_design_mini_sweep_v1/results*/
# finished runs are tracked records with the steady-state v4 contract (summary with the frames manifest, execution lock, run state,
# status/series/maps, final checkpoint metadata + npz sidecars, the sealed protocol copy); frames, checkpoint arrays, the field
# anchor, the raw series and logs/pid stay untracked; every OTHER per-design directory under results/ (running or scratch) stays
# ignored so a job worktree remains clean. 047 launch 1 = plateau record (canonical directory). 056 launch 1 = triad-gate stop on
# the pre-v2.0.4 RAW single-node omega_pe dt statistic, archived as -launch1-triad-gate-stop/ (+ triad-stop-diagnosis.json) so
# that launch 2 (amended gate reading) runs in the canonical directory.
!modern/experiments/pic2d_design_mini_sweep_v1/results/
